| 9 | K&R C established in 1978 book | **0.88** | [3] |
| 10 | ANSI C standardized in 1989 | **0.88** | [3] |

---

## Conclusion

The C programming language was created by **Dennis Ritchie** at **Bell Labs**, with development spanning **1969 to 1973** and the language reaching its recognizable form around **1972**. It was designed to make Unix portable across hardware platforms, drawing on the earlier B and BCPL languages. C went on to become one of the most influential programming languages in history, formalized first by the K&R book in 1978 and later by the ANSI C standard in 1989.

